---
title: "GRØD"
template: editorial
spreads:
  - heading: "Notes, not transcripts"
    body: "A transcript is evidence. The note is the point. Every meeting becomes one continuous, editable document. Summary, decisions, actions, sitting right beside anything I typed myself. GRØD enriches it; it never owns it."
    image: "/shots/grod/briefing.webp"
    alt: "A meeting note in GRØD, headed 'Weekly product review', holding the story, the decisions and the risks, with a question about the meeting answered inline and stamped with the minute it was said."
  - heading: "Remembers people, not speaker labels"
    body: "Voices persist across meetings, connected to real people, merged when needed, forgotten on purpose if I ask. Pick a few people and see every meeting they share."
    image: "/shots/grod/people.webp"
    alt: "GRØD's People view, listing everyone due in today's meetings by name, with one attendee marked 'Not in People' and waiting to be matched."
  - heading: "Search that closes the loop"
    body: "Search covers notes, decisions, actions, people, and full transcripts, then jumps straight to the moment something was said. Ask a question across meetings and get an answer with a citation, not a guess."
    image: "/shots/grod/search.webp"
    alt: "A search for 'confidence ribbon decision' in GRØD, returning the two people who discussed it and the two meetings where it was decided, the decision quoted in place."
  - heading: "Calendar-aware, not calendar-first"
    body: "GRØD knows what's on my calendar, so a scheduled meeting strengthens what it's already noticing: join links, event context, a quiet dock before things start. But time alone never triggers a recording."
    image: "/shots/grod/agenda.webp"
    alt: "GRØD's agenda, with the next meeting docked at the top thirty minutes ahead of time and a record button waiting to be pressed, above the week's earlier meetings."
---

GRØD notices a meeting, records it quietly on my Mac, and turns it into a note I'd actually want to keep. Not a transcript, and not something that forgets who was in the room.
